      "id": "GLU-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "A prescribed determinant between two integral lattices",
      "anchor": "inputs-lattice-prescribed",
      "statement": "For finite J and coordinate lattices Λ(a),Λ(b) in F^J, a determinant β∈F× is realized by an F-linear map onto Λ(b) precisely when ord_P β equals the total target minus source order at every finite prime P, with β=1 if J is empty. The sufficient direction is the SStein statement; the necessity follows by taking top exterior powers.",
      "hypotheses": "Number field F, its ring of integers, finite index set J, finitely supported integral divisors a_j,b_j over the height-one primes, β≠0. The construction over the nonempty block chooses a distinguished coordinate; the empty block uses the identity.",
