      "id": "GLU-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "The selected determinant belongs to a regrouped block",
      "anchor": "inputs-lattice-blocks",
      "statement": "For the two-dimensional index set over Z/q the Galois twists merge the distinguished slope's κ-orbit at label 1. The total ideal order equals ord_P β there and equals zero elsewhere. Gluing produces F-linear blocks with the prescribed determinants and L′-linear maps g_t carrying the same standard lattice onto the same target at every slope.",
      "hypotheses": "q=ℓ^ν; cyclic Galois number-field layer F/L′, primitive ζ of order q, γζ=ζ^(1+ℓ^c), ord γ=ℓ^(ν−c), 1≤c≤ν and c≥2 if ℓ=2. The finite relation has a unit coefficient at t₀. The interpolating divisor data meet the specialized cGtEq and cGtNe identities. For cJoin the internal degree is 2a+3<ℓ^c (book degree 2e+1 with a=e−1).",
