      "id": "GLU-03",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "From the integral stabilizer to ordinary GL with compatible reduction",
      "anchor": "inputs-lattice-stabilize",
      "statement": "The common carriers in GLoc have ratios g_t^{-1}g_t₀ in the integral stabilizer H. A group homology cycle in H pushes to one in GL_N(O_L′) by extending the action on the finite projective M=(O_F)^J trivially to a complement in a finite free module. Its period under every admissible reduction agrees with the unstabilized residue evaluation.",
      "hypotheses": "B∈O_L′ nonzero covers divisor support and a splitting denominator. The test uses r:O_F→k to a finite field, r(B)≠0, surjective on O_L′ and the given root, character and additive cycle functional. The universal CFree takes any finite projective R-module, a surjective residue map R→k, a semilinear surjection π with kernel inside ker(r)M and compatible group action. CInt supplies these data at split test maps.",
