  "outstanding": [
    "The fractional-ideal factorization and comaximal two-generator theorem over a Dedekind domain are used as algebraic suppliers.",
    "SDN-01–02 derive the denominator, split residue coordinates and localization at the divisor support needed for CJoin. The cyclic filling, interpolation, gluing and evaluation have separate reconstructions.",
    "The finite free rank N of an individual detection cycle is existential. The later uniform torsion rank is determined by homological stability at a common size, not by this lattice lemma."
  ],
  "review_scope": "Independent review of the determinant-one moves, equality of the valuation sums, the rational example, the Galois label regrouping and the free and residue splittings. The distinction between the global fields F and L′, the localizations and the residue test is explicit."
}
